    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="1372" n="1356" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/2–2751: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-02-27">February 27,
                        1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3732. Reference Embtel 3727, repeated Torquay
                    2 February 26. Foreign Office advises that as result of Embassy’s approach
                    yesterday another telegram was sent last night to Di Nola instructing him try
                    his best find workable compromise on Benelux
                    memorandum, meeting at least in part desires of US delegation, while always
                    bearing in mind Italian adherence to principles of Pella Plan.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 3732, repeated Torquay 3, information Paris 514.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dunn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
